- **Do not adopt Option A unconditionally.** The variable-wise amendment as specified would remove the only detector of a real negation-scope ambiguity in the WCC formal sentence. The correct fix is Option B *or* Option A′ (variable-wise **plus** a scope/grouping check that requires composite binders whose variables appear in a negated clause to be rendered as a single grouped term, e.g. `(q,t0)` or `q,t0` under one quantifier).

